course: dictionary
lesson: 6074
title: Words from the desert
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing you can see, like a tree. Others can name the same thing in a different way. Read the words around the new word, because they are its context. «Many desert plants, like cactuses, have shallow roots that spread wide to catch rain before it dries.» Desert, plants, roots and rain are the clues, so a desert plant grows where rain is rare.
explain: Now read: «a mesquite root was reported over 50 metres deep.» Roots, deep and metres are clues that mesquite is a plant. A mesquite grows in dry lands, and its roots go very deep to find water.
explain: Mesquite can also mean the wood of the tree. In «mesquite-grilled» food, the food was cooked over mesquite wood. The word cooked, and the smoky flavour it gives, tells you it is the wood, not the plant. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: A mesquite is a spiny shrub or small tree of the pea family.
fact: Mesquite grows in deserts and dry lands of the south-western USA and Mexico.
fact: The wood of mesquite gives a smoky flavour to barbecued food.
fact: Mesquite has long seed pods, and native peoples ground them into flour.
fact: Some mesquite roots can go over 50 metres deep to reach water.
exercise: «a mesquite root was reported over 50 metres deep.» What does mesquite mean here? | A kind of sea creature | *A desert plant whose roots reach deep water | A metal used for tools | A loud type of music
exercise: «The steak was grilled over mesquite and tasted smoky.» What is mesquite in this sentence? | A type of bread | *The wood that gives a smoky flavour | A desert town | A cooking pot
exercise: Which word in «Many desert plants, like cactuses, have shallow roots» tells you that mesquite is a plant? | rain | shallow | cactuses | *plants
test: Where does mesquite grow? | *Deserts and dry lands of the south-western USA and Mexico | Wet rainforests of South America | Cold beaches of northern Europe | Frozen mountains of Canada
test: Mesquite was brought to Australia and is now a harmful weed. What is mesquite in Australia? | A tasty fruit | *A plant that causes harm as a weed | A kind of kangaroo | A desert river
exam: Which sentence uses mesquite to mean the wood? | Mesquite pods were long and brown in the summer. | *The brisket was cooked over mesquite and tasted smoky. | Mesquite roots reached water far below the sand. | The mesquite grew on the dry hill for many years.
